{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And two men remained.</b> Of those who were chosen — they said: We are not worthy of this greatness (see Sanhedrin 17)." "<b>And they were among those written down.</b> Among the selected for the Sanhedrin. And all of them were inscribed by name and by lot, because the tally comes to twelve tribes — six and six for every single tribe, apart from two tribes that receive only five and five. Moses said: No tribe will accept me to subtract even one elder from its tribe. What did he do? He took 72 slips and wrote on seventy of them 'elder' and on two of them 'blank,' and he selected from each and every tribe six, making 72. He said to them: Draw your slips from within the box. Whoever drew 'elder' in his hand was consecrated. Whoever drew 'blank' in his hand, he said to him: The Omnipresent does not want you. (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 17)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:27.514986932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}